    "description": "Vintage Waterman Laureat Marble Grey and Gold Tone Trim Fountain Pen IOB\nApproximate Measurements:\n5.25\" long (closed)\nCondition:\nNo visible scratches\nNotes:\nNote: Any extra props (i.e., stands, mannequins, etc.) are not part of the auction and are for presentation purposes only.\nUsed Items Disclaimer:\nThis is a pre-owned item and is being sold \"AS IS \" If you have any questions concerning this item, feel free to contact us.\nWe describe our items to the best of our ability and try to incorporate as much research as possible with books andInternet, however, we are not experts in any field.\nGoodwill Industries of the Chesapeake, Inc. prepares people to secure and retain employment to build successfulindependent lives.\nThank you for your support!\n*All gold is tested using a Niton DXL Precious metal Analyzer (x-ray technology)\n*All silver is tested using a magnet, acid, or x-raytechnology.\n*Gemstones are tested using a SmartPro Gem-Eye 1 gemstone tester. Our gem tester does not distinguish between real and synthetic gems.\n*We DO have the ability to determine genuine diamonds from simulated diamonds such as cubic zirconia, moissanite, zircon, white sapphire, white spinel, white topaz and other diamond imitations.\n*We cannot determine the nature of \"turquoise\" stones, and sometimes, turquoise refers to the \"color of\".\n*We do not have the ability to determine the nature of a pearl (if it is \"natural\" vs cultivated). If it is fake, it will be labeled FAUX. If it may be natural or cultivated, it will be called genuine.\n*Due to our items being donated, we are unable to guarantee the continued functionality of any watch after listing, however, if the watch does run at the time of listing, it will be mentioned.\nBuyer verification:\nIf the current bid on an item is higher than average, and we are unable to confirm your account, your bid may be retracted for this reason.",
