    "description": "Artist Unknown\nNatural Agate Geode Slice Set\nPolished Stone with Copper Foil Edging\n6.5\" x 5.5\"\nUnsigned\nThis collection of six natural agate geode slices showcases a sophisticated array of geological formations, featuring intricate banding and crystalline centers in a palette of warm ochre, sienna, and translucent cream. Four specimens are enhanced with a hand-applied copper foil perimeter, a technique that provides a modern, metallic contrast to the organic, rugged textures of the stone's exterior. The slices demonstrate characteristic chalcedony layering and varied mineral density, typical of high-quality volcanic geodes.\nSet includes four copper-foiled slices and two natural specimens with varied finishes\nTranslucent centers exhibit excellent light transmission, revealing fine internal structures\nIdeal for use as decorative coasters, display specimens, or lapidary art bases\nLargest piece measures approximately 6.5\" x 5.5\" x 1\"\nCondition:\nGood pre-owned condition. The stones exhibit natural surface variations, inclusions, and minor internal fissures typical of geological specimens. The copper foil shows light oxidation and surface wear at the edges but remains structurally secure. One specimen is partially unfinished.\nThank you for all of your support!",
